<#ftl output_format="HTML" auto_esc=true>
<#-- These feature values come from native ReactiveTogglyClient.evaluateAll().
     The empty map is used only by the visibly unconfigured setup shell. -->
<#macro badge value><span class="badge ${value?then('on','off')}">${value?then('ON','OFF')}</span></#macro>
<#macro presets><div class="presets"><form method="post" action="/context"><button name="preset" value="matching">Matching preset</button></form><form method="post" action="/context"><button name="preset" value="nonmatching">Non-matching preset</button></form></div></#macro>
<#macro table keys><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Flag key</th><th>Definition</th><th>This request</th></tr></thead><tbody><#list keys as key><tr data-flag="${key}"><td><code>${key}</code></td><td>${definitions?seq_contains(key)?then('Present','Absent')}</td><td><@badge value=(features[key])!false/><#if key == 'filter-device-type'> <small>Macintosh detection unsupported in 1.5.1</small></#if></td></tr></#list></tbody></table></div></#macro>
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"><title>${title} · Java Spring WebFlux SDK Sample</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css"><script src="/workshop.js" defer></script></head><body>
<header><p class="eyebrow">TOGGLY / JAVA SPRING WEBFLUX</p><a class="brand" href="/">Feature flag workshop</a><p>Learn native Spring WebFlux, one request at a time.</p></header>
<nav aria-label="Sections"><#list paths as link><a href="${link}">${titles[link?index]}</a></#list></nav><main>
<#if !configured><aside class="warning" role="status"><strong>Missing TOGGLY_APP_KEY — unconfigured offline mode.</strong> No live evaluations or synthetic enabled flags. Protected examples deny with 503. <a href="/configuration">Set up your app</a>.</aside>
<#else><aside class="status">Signed definitions configured · ${definitions?size} current definitions · HTTP poll every 60 seconds in normal startup. Reload to see current evaluations.</aside><#if definitions?size == 0><aside class="warning">No definitions available yet. Missing flags use false defaults; check your key, environment and connection.</aside></#if></#if>
<#if errors gt 0><aside class="warning">SDK refresh errors observed: ${errors}. The SDK retains its last valid signed definitions. This cumulative warning remains after recovery; inspect current flags and retry refresh.</aside></#if>
<p class="context">User: <strong>${identity?has_content?then(identity,'anonymous')}</strong> · Order: <strong>${order}</strong> · Demo identities are not authentication.</p><h1>${title}</h1>
<#switch path>
<#case '/'>
<p>Follow the sections from a Boolean flag to isolated users, Orders and native reactive route gates.</p><div class="cards"><#list paths as link><#if link != '/' ><a class="card" href="${link}"><span>${link?index}</span><h2>${titles[link?index]}</h2></a></#if></#list></div>
<h2>First flag exercise</h2><ol><li>Complete Configuration and create <code>new-dashboard</code> in Production.</li><li>Enable it, wait up to 60 seconds or use Refresh in Spring WebFlux integration.</li><li>Open Declarative gates: the feature route allows and the negate route denies.</li><li>Disable the flag, refresh, and observe the opposite behavior.</li></ol>
<h2>Flag checklist and current snapshot</h2><p>When configured, native reactive client evaluates these flags for this request before the template renders. Absent means the key is missing from current definitions, not simply OFF.</p><@table keys=flags/><p><a href="/api/evaluate">Programmatic JSON snapshot</a></p>
<#break>
<#case '/gates'>
<p>The native <code>FeatureGateFilter</code> uses its <code>pathMatcher</code> extension with compiled Spring <code>PathPattern</code> objects. Encoded segments and matrix parameters identify the same route as controller dispatch; encoded slashes stay within their segment. Spring orders it after the context filter and offloading boundary; configured gates deny with 404 by default.</p>
<div class="cards"><article class="card"><h2>Feature</h2><@badge value=(features['new-dashboard'])!false/><p><a href="/gated/feature">Try feature route</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>Negate</h2><@badge value=configured && !((features['new-dashboard'])!false)/><p><a href="/gated/negate">Try negate route</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>ALL: dashboard + API v2</h2><@badge value=allOn/><p><a href="/gated/all">Try ALL route</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>ANY: dashboard + API v2</h2><@badge value=anyOn/><p><a href="/gated/any">Try ANY route</a></p></article></div>
<h2>Real template integration</h2>
<#-- FreeMarker branches use the actual native reactive client's features map, not a sample evaluator. -->
<#if (features['new-dashboard'])!false><p id="dashboard-content">New dashboard content is visible.</p><#else><p id="dashboard-content">Classic dashboard fallback is visible.</p></#if>
<p>The controller awaits <code>ReactiveTogglyClient.evaluateAll()</code> and supplies <code>features</code>. This FreeMarker condition is ordinary view composition; the SDK owns the evaluation. Hiding HTML is not an access-control boundary: the native route gate checks again before the action.</p>
<h2>Variants</h2><aside class="note">Native variant allocation is unsupported in io.toggly core/WebFlux 1.5.1. No variant is fabricated. <code>switchOn</code> selects between two caller-provided publishers using a Boolean flag; telemetry variant labels do not allocate experiments.</aside>
<#break>
<#case '/programmatic'>
<p>Native publishers read subscription-local Reactor context. Offload each potentially cold call, including after an async boundary; the wrapper delegates to the synchronous core.</p><pre>Mono.defer(() -&gt; reactive.isEnabled("api-v2"))
    .subscribeOn(Schedulers.boundedElastic());
reactive.allEnabled(List.of("new-dashboard", "api-v2"));
reactive.evaluateAll();
reactive.switchOn("api-v2", Mono.just("v2"), Mono.just("v1"));</pre>
<p>The app wraps each call above in its <code>offload</code> helper. Current API version: <strong>${apiVersion}</strong></p><p><a href="/api/evaluate">Open delayed request JSON</a> · <a href="/api/flag/unknown">Unknown flag defaults false</a></p><form method="post" action="/actions/submit"><button>Try enhanced submit</button></form><p>A native <code>FeatureGateFilter</code> protects this action with status 403. The handler demonstrates <code>ifEnabled</code> with a lazy action publisher; no order is persisted. Unconfigured actions return 503.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/identity'>
<p>A session stores demo inputs, never evaluated flag results. <code>DemoContextResolver.resolve</code> constructs immutable identity, claims, request fields and Order before native gates or reactive evaluation.</p><@presets/>
<h2>Customize this session</h2><form class="fields" method="post" action="/context"><label>Identity<input name="identity" maxlength="512" value="${identity}"></label><label>Claim role<input name="role" maxlength="512" value="${role}"></label><label>Country<input name="country" maxlength="512" value="${country}"></label><label>Accept-Language<input name="language" maxlength="512" value="${language}"></label><label>User-Agent<input name="userAgent" maxlength="512" value="${userAgent}"></label><label>Order<select name="order"><option value="vip"<#if order == 'ord-vip'> selected</#if>>ord-vip</option><option value="standard"<#if order != 'ord-vip'> selected</#if>>ord-standard</option></select></label><button>Apply session context</button></form><form method="post" action="/context"><button name="preset" value="clear">Clear session identity</button></form>
<p>Initial anonymous requests read actual User-Agent, Accept-Language and cf-ipcountry headers where present. Presets deliberately override these fields. These local controls are not trusted authentication; in a deployed app derive identity and claims from authenticated server state, and country from a trusted proxy.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/orders'>
<p>User identity stays the same while the entity changes. These checks run side by side in one request using <code>context.withEntity(...)</code>, with kind Order, Id, Vip and Total.</p><div class="cards"><article class="card"><h2>ord-vip · Vip=true</h2><span id="vip-result"><@badge value=vipOn/></span><p><a href="/orders?order=vip">Select VIP for this request</a></p></article><article class="card"><h2>ord-standard · Vip=false</h2><span id="standard-result"><@badge value=standardOn/></span><p><a href="/orders?order=standard">Select standard for this request</a></p></article></div><p>Without an entity: <span id="missing-result"><@badge value=missingOn/></span> · <a href="/orders?order=missing">Try missing entity</a></p><pre>var order = new TogglyEntityContext("Order", "ord-vip",
    Map.of("Id", "ord-vip", "Vip", true, "Total", 250));
reactive.isEnabled("ExpressCheckout", context.withEntity(order))
    .subscribeOn(Schedulers.boundedElastic());</pre><p>Never reuse a Boolean result across different Orders. The published engine compares attributes without enforcing definition.contextKind; this app explicitly constructs Order at its boundary. A missing entity evaluates false.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/filters'>
<p>All eleven rows use the native reactive client and real installed SDK. Apply a saved preset or compare one request without changing your session.</p><@presets/><p><a href="/filters?preset=matching">Matching for this request</a> · <a href="/filters?preset=nonmatching">Non-matching for this request</a></p><@table keys=filters/>
<p>AlwaysOn stays ON for both; TimeWindow stays ON during 2020–2099. Percentage is sticky per identity and flag, so Alice/Bob are not prescribed ON/OFF. The seven other supported segment/context rows should be ON for Matching and OFF for Non-matching. DeviceType Macintosh is a native SDK gap: the parser recognizes iPhone/iPad/iPod but returns Other for desktop Macintosh. The exact shared rule remains OFF.</p><p>Matching: alice, role=admin, US, Chrome/en, Macintosh device, Mac OS, VIP Order. Non-matching: bob, role=user, CA, Firefox/fr, Windows, standard Order. Identity shows all exact request fields.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/webflux'>
<h2>Native reactive pipeline</h2><ol><li>Startup preloads signed definitions on the startup thread before Reactor Netty accepts requests.</li><li>Spring sorts native <code>TogglyContextFilter</code>, order -100, with the sample asynchronous <code>ReactiveContextResolver</code>.</li><li>A deferred <code>boundedElastic</code> filter, order -90, protects the synchronous native gate from a cold snapshot fetch.</li><li>A sample missing-key guard, order -80, denies protected examples.</li><li>Native <code>FeatureGateFilter</code> beans, order 0, use Spring parsed route matchers and evaluate flags using native Reactor context.</li><li>The controller uses the real <code>ReactiveTogglyClient</code> bean, including after delayed scheduler boundaries; each potentially cold call is offloaded again.</li><li>Reactor context belongs to the subscription. Completion, error and cancellation do not install user state on shared threads.</li><li>Shutdown stops the listener and cancels tracked accepted connections, closes Spring, then closes the sole owned core client and its HTTP provider/polling scheduler.</li></ol>
<p><a href="/gated/beta">Try native beta-access gate</a> · <a href="/native/reactive">Try delayed native identity/Boolean check</a> · <a href="/native/enabled">Native enabledFeatures Flux</a></p><pre>Mono.delay(Duration.ofMillis(15))
    .then(TogglyContextFilter.getContext())
    .flatMap(ctx -&gt; Mono.defer(() -&gt; reactive.isEnabled("filter-targeting"))
        .subscribeOn(Schedulers.boundedElastic()));</pre>
<form data-native-refresh method="post" action="/api/refresh"><button>Request native definitions refresh</button></form><output id="refresh-result" aria-live="polite"></output><p>The native <code>reactive.refresh()</code> offloads internally. Completion can retain the prior snapshot after an error. Return Home to inspect current flags and the cumulative warning.</p>
<h2>Cancellation and ownership</h2><p>Do not call block() inside request handlers or use ContextHolder. Cancelling a subscriber stops downstream delivery and queued work, but an already running synchronous HTTP fetch may continue until it finishes or times out. Offloading protects the event loop; it does not convert the transport into cancellable nonblocking I/O. The shared client remains alive for other requests and closes once on application shutdown.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/configuration'>
<h2>Connect your own application</h2><ol><li>Open app.toggly.io and select workspace <strong>Toggly Samples</strong>.</li><li>Create <strong>Java Spring WebFlux SDK Sample</strong>; select <strong>Java</strong> technology and <strong>Production</strong> environment.</li><li>Add allowed origins <code>http://localhost:8089</code> and <code>http://127.0.0.1:8089</code>.</li><li>Add Order with Id string key, Vip boolean and Total optional number.</li><li>Create all sixteen flags and the Filters category using the README recipe. Java’s picker omits Percentage, Targeting and TimeWindow; the README gives the authorized management API fallback for those three rules.</li><li>Copy .env.example to .env, set your key locally, export it, and restart.</li></ol><p>Never commit a real key. The missing-key app makes no Toggly requests and has no synthetic live data.</p><h2>Loading, refresh and errors</h2><p>Startup attempts signed definitions. Unknown flags default false. The native provider can fetch again on empty snapshots, polls every 60 seconds and retains last valid definitions after network or signature failures. Pages reevaluate the current context; results are never stored in sessions. Initial unavailable definitions show a warning rather than claiming live OFF is confirmed.</p><p>Tests use the real HTTP provider against isolated signed loopback definitions with temporary cryptographic keys. Those fixtures are not in the production package. Live dashboard setup has not been verified.</p>
<#break>
<#case '/allowed'><p>The published FeatureGateFilter allowed this request before the controller ran.</p><@table keys=flags/><#break>
</#switch>
</main><footer>Published io.toggly 1.5.1 · Spring WebFlux 7.0.9 · FreeMarker 2.3.35 · Reactor Netty 1.3.7 · Java 26</footer></body></html>
